      "side": 1,
      "message": "[From Jetski review] Quoting `before`, `after`, and the argument value separately and then concatenating them can produce adjacent quotes like `\"hello \"\"world foo\"` (when both `before` and the value contain spaces), which Windows `CommandLineToArgvW` interprets as a literal `\"` rather than quote concatenation. It also behaves unexpectedly when the format string itself wraps `%s` in quotes (e.g. `format \u003d \u0027--foo\u003d\"%s\"\u0027`).\n\nWould it be simpler and more accurate to apply `Formatter` / `join_with` on the unescaped strings first, and call `escape_ninja_token` once on the final assembled token?",
