      "side": 1,
      "message": "[From Jetski review] Two things to consider here:\n1. Line 27 escapes `\\\\` when quoting is enabled, but `b\u0027\\\\\u0027` is not checked in `escape_mode`. A token like `foo\\bar` (without spaces or quotes) will not have its backslash escaped, whereas `foo\\bar baz` will become `\"foo\\\\bar baz\"`.\n2. Escaping `$` as `$$` only escapes it for Ninja, so Ninja passes a literal `$` to `/bin/sh -c`, which will still expand `$BAR` / `$USER` as shell environment variables (unlike `EscapeStringToString_PosixNinjaFork` in `src/gn/escape.cc` which emits `\\$$`). Is shell variable expansion intended here?",
